WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.330
Seal the end of a syringe full of air,

2
00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:05.250
so nothing can get in or out.

3
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.390
Now push the plunger in slowly,

4
00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:10.010
squashing the air into half the space.

5
00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:13.330
The air pushes back on
your thumb twice as hard.

6
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.910
You haven't added a
single particle of air.

7
00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:17.890
The temperature hasn't changed.

8
00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:21.110
So why does the squashed
air push back harder?

9
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:24.310
In this mission, you'll picture
a gas as particles moving

10
00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.100
randomly at high speed.

11
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:28.570
You'll find out what
causes gas pressure,

12
00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:32.890
and how squashing a gas or
heating it changes that pressure.

13
00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:37.450
Your mission: explain why squashing
a gas raises its pressure.
